&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Impact on our Mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zocdoc&#39;s most important asset is our people. As Senior Benefits Associate, you&#39;ll play a meaningful role in making sure that every Zocdoc employee can access, understand, and rely on the benefits they need — so they can show up and do their best work helping patients get the care they deserve. You&#39;ll own the day-to-day operations of our health, retirement, and leave programs with precision and genuine care, while continuously finding ways to make our benefits experience more seamless, equitable, and exceptional. This is a role where operational excellence meets real human impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll enjoy this role if you are…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personally motivated by building programs and experiences that genuinely support people — you see great benefits administration as an act of care, not just compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Autonomous, urgent, and creative - you genuinely love solving problems and creating lasting solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized and detail-oriented — you catch data integrity issues before they become problems, and you track every open thread to closure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about the employee experience and committed to making every benefits interaction feel personal and high-touch, not transactional&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The kind of person who builds strong, trust-based partnerships across Payroll, Finance, and external vendors — because you know that great benefits outcomes depend on great relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serious about your work, but not about yourself. You take pride in your work while remaining humble, adaptable, and approachable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your day to day is…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administering Zocdoc&#39;s employee benefit programs — medical, dental, vision, life, disability, wellness, FSAs, HSAs, COBRA, retirement, commuter, and voluntary benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serving as the primary point of contact for employees navigating benefits questions, qualifying life events, new hire enrollments, terminations, and dependent verification — delivering a high-touch experience at every step&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administering leave of absence programs in partnership with Zocdoc&#39;s leave administrator, including FMLA, ADA, state leave programs, paid family leave, workers&#39; compensation, and short-term disability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performing regular audits of benefit eligibility, payroll deductions, vendor files, invoices, and system integrations to maintain data integrity and financial accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconciling monthly benefit invoices and partnering with Payroll and Finance to resolve discrepancies quickly and accurately&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting annual Open Enrollment from system configuration testing through employee education sessions and post-enrollment auditing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintaining compliance with ERISA, ACA, COBRA, HIPAA, Section 125, Medicare reporting, and applicable federal, state, and local regulations — and supporting Form 5500 filings, nondiscrimination testing, and other annual activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing and maintaining employee-facing documentation, benefit guides, and knowledge articles that make our programs easy to understand and navigate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifying opportunities to automate processes, leverage AI tools, improve reporting, and continuously elevate the overall employee experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
