&lt;li&gt;Meaningful (4–6 years) of progressive benefits administration experience, ideally gained in a high-growth, fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to integrate generative AI tools into daily workflows to automate tasks, foster innovation, and maximize productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience administering Leave of Absence programs, including FMLA, ADA, state leave programs, and disability benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong working knowledge of federal and state benefits regulations — COBRA, HIPAA, FMLA, ERISA, ACA — and the confidence to interpret and apply them accurately&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A compassionate but consultative approach with employees and vendors, with the communication skills to make complex benefits topics feel accessible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superb attention to detail and organizational skills — you believe accurate data is the foundation of a trustworthy benefits program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent relevant experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced benefits and/or HR certifications (CEBS, SHRM-CP, PHR) are a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
