&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Impact on our Mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re building a world class Marketing team at Zocdoc -- and we’re growing fast! As an Associate Web Developer, you&#39;ll own the technical development and health of Zocdoc&#39;s provider-facing website — a core channel that helps connect healthcare providers with millions of patients. The ideal candidate is a strong full-stack WordPress developer who brings deep knowledge of web best practices, a point of view on site reliability and security, and a solid understanding of website architecture. You research before you build, care about doing things the right way, and can make sound technical decisions independently. It&#39;s a great opportunity for a thoughtful, technically rigorous developer to make a big impact on a highly visible part of the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll enjoy this role if you are...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious about trying new things, challenging assumptions, and solving problems in creative ways&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited by the challenge of owning a live production web property end-to-end — from updates to full builds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to see the big picture and translate high-level marketing strategy into clean, performant technical solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly collaborative and comfortable working with cross-functional teams across Marketing, Design, Data, and external agencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serious about your work, but not about yourself — this team moves fast and has a sense of humor about it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your day to day is…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building, maintaining, and improving Zocdoc&#39;s provider-facing website, including CMS configuration, content architecture, and hosting environment management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing and maintaining custom components, templates, and page structures that support marketing campaigns and the provider acquisition funnel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing and optimizing Marketo form integrations and lead capture flows across the site&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embedding and configuring Wistia video assets and ensuring seamless performance across pages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with designers and PMMs to implement new landing pages, content updates, and site redesigns on tight timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting A/B testing initiatives by implementing front-end changes, tracking code, and experiment variations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conducting QA across browsers and devices, resolving bugs, and proactively identifying performance or UX issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to documentation, code quality standards, and scalable development practices for the web team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll be successful in this role if you are…&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bringing 4–7 years of professional web development experience, with meaningful time owning a production CMS-backed marketing site end-to-end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced across one or more modern CMS platforms (WordPress, Contentful, Sanity, Prismic, or similar) with the ability to evaluate, recommend, and migrate between them as business needs evolve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with CMS hosting and infrastructure best practices (staging environments, deployment workflows, caching, CDN)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in front-end development: HTML5, CSS3/SCSS, JavaScript (vanilla and/or jQuery), and responsive/mobile-first design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with backend web development: REST APIs, webhooks, and CMS-specific extensibility patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced integrating third-party martech tools — particularly Marketo (forms, tracking, lead flows) and Wistia (video embeds and analytics)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled at debugging cross-browser and performance issues and translating them into clean fixes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear communicator who can scope, estimate, and execute independently with minimal oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus: experience with Figma handoffs, analytics/tag management, and working in agile marketing environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An incredible team of smart and supportive people&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A competitive compensation package, including attractive medical insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Amazing perks – think catered lunch every day, Ping Pong, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Daycare/creche facility for kids&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The chance to create a better healthcare experience for millions of patients!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Corporate wellness programs with Headspace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cellphone and wifi reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sabbatical leave (over 5 years)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual sponsored health check-ups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Zocdoc is certified as a Great Place to Work 2025-2026&lt;/li&gt;
