&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll enjoy this role if you are…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited about designing and building strategic data products that drive impactful outcomes across the entire organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about solving complex, high-impact problems using data and analytics at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Committed to setting a high bar for technical excellence and continuously improving whatever you&#39;re working on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative leader who enjoys working cross-functionally in a supportive and highly cooperative environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enthusiastic about architecting scalable data solutions using cutting-edge technologies to support long-term business strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Your day to day is…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Defining and enabling trusted, strategic datasets and analytics solutions that empower data consumers to quickly and reliably gain insights at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading efforts to enhance self-serve analytics across the organization through advanced administration, adoption strategies, and training for analytics tools (Looker and Amplitude)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering strategically with analysts, product managers, and product engineers to ensure the analytics infrastructure meets evolving business requirements and is robust and maintainable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architecting and developing production-grade data transformations and models using SQL, DBT, and Dagster, ensuring optimal performance, maintainability, scalability, and reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating closely with data engineering on strategic infrastructure initiatives to enhance data ingestion, processing pipelines, and integration of new data sources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driving the establishment and continuous improvement of standards around data governance, security, privacy, quality, and retention, influencing best practices across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll be successful in this role if you have…&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience as an analytics engineer, data engineer, or similar role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience using DBT &amp;amp; DBT Core, with a strong understanding of data modeling and data warehousing concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in writing performant SQL, especially within cloud-based data warehouses like Snowflake, and have strong Looker developer skills, with an emphasis on LookML modeling and overall project design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing the administration and/or adoption of data visualization tools (e.g. Looker) and event-based analytics/user journey tools (e.g. Amplitude)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to navigate ambiguity and work with urgency in a fast-moving environment with multiple stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good communication skills across all levels of stakeholders (business &amp;amp; technical) with the ability to influence and build consensus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Python&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Dagster or other orchestration tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience utilizing AI Codegen to improve the efficiency of your workflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data governance principles, KPI management, and supporting data operations for business intelligence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
